    { math: '2 · The poverty-of-stimulus argument', note: 'Children hear imperfect, finite speech yet acquire infinite, systematic grammar — Chomsky\'s argument that the machinery must be partly innate (universal grammar). The most contested claim in the field (constructionists reply: general learning + rich input suffices).' },
